Here's a nice dinner party script in Java that introduces and greets some famous figures:
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class DinnerParty {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayList<Figure> guests = new ArrayList<Figure>();
        guests.add(new Figure("Albert Einstein"));
        guests.add(new Figure("Leonardo da Vinci"));
        guests.add(new Figure("Marie Curie"));

        for (Figure f : guests) {
            System.out.println("Hello, " + f.name + ". It is a pleasure to have you at my dinner.");
        }
    }
}
private class Figure {
    public String name;
    public Figure(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }
}
```
This program creates a virtual dinner party where you can interact with famous historical figures like Albert Einstein, Leonardo da Vinci, and Marie Curie. Running this code would be like having a conversation with these guests, making dinner preparations or engaging in meaningful discussions about their fields of expertise. It offers a fun and unique way to explore history and celebrate these significant figures.
